<section class="product-roadmap">
  <h2 class="product-section-title">How to get in</h2>
  <ol class="product-roadmap-list">
    <li class="product-roadmap-item">
      <p class="product-roadmap-phase">Step 1</p>
      <h3 class="product-roadmap-title">Join the closed beta</h3>
      <p class="product-roadmap-desc">
        Leave your email above and we'll send your invite when there's room. We let people in a few at a time, so this
        is the step that starts the clock.
      </p>
    </li>
    <li class="product-roadmap-item">
      <p class="product-roadmap-phase">Step 2</p>
      <h3 class="product-roadmap-title">Install Guido from your invite</h3>
      <p class="product-roadmap-desc">
        Your invite points at the Google Play listing. It isn't public during the beta yet, so install from the link we
        send rather than from a search.
      </p>
    </li>
    <li class="product-roadmap-item">
      <p class="product-roadmap-phase">Step 3</p>
      <h3 class="product-roadmap-title">Turn on GT7 telemetry</h3>
      <p class="product-roadmap-desc">
        In Gran Turismo 7 on your PS5, enable telemetry in the game settings. That's how Guido reads the car — no
        cables, no extra hardware.
      </p>
    </li>
    <li class="product-roadmap-item">
      <p class="product-roadmap-phase">Step 4</p>
      <h3 class="product-roadmap-title">Mount the phone and launch</h3>
      <p class="product-roadmap-desc">
        Put the phone or tablet on the same home network, best mounted beside your wheel, and open Guido. It finds your
        sim session on the network by itself.
      </p>
    </li>
  </ol>
</section>

